{"assets":["/statement-assets/edcf819620daca4e850c396dcbc2cc542468f651d8a8656cdf007aa1c5ab72f6.png","/statement-assets/902ce2fb66aff696e6d4d480375771d203e8b0b89bb6856d5a0920fff8d3efc8.png","/statement-assets/eff3ee278eb117d93ae68f5a9deb8c25aeba4c43de40adcb0feedb8480477357.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1098","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. Construct a tree"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Misha walked through the snowy forest and he was so fascinated by the trees to decide to draw his own tree!"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Misha would like to construct a rooted tree with $$$n$$$ vertices, indexed from 1 to $$$n$$$, where the root has index 1. Every other vertex has a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"parent"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$p_i$$$, and $$$i$$$ is called a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"child"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of vertex $$$p_i$$$. Vertex $$$u$$$ belongs to the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"subtree"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of vertex $$$v$$$ iff $$$v$$$ is reachable from $$$u$$$ while iterating over the parents ($$$u$$$, $$$p_{u}$$$, $$$p_{p_{u}}$$$, ...). Clearly, $$$v$$$ belongs to its own subtree, and the number of vertices in the subtree is called the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"size"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of the subtree. Misha is only interested in trees where every vertex belongs to the subtree of vertex $$$1$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Below there is a tree with $$$6$$$ vertices. The subtree of vertex $$$2$$$ contains vertices $$$2$$$, $$$3$$$, $$$4$$$, $$$5$$$. Hence the size of its subtree is $$$4$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/edcf819620daca4e850c396dcbc2cc542468f651d8a8656cdf007aa1c5ab72f6.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"branching coefficient"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of the tree is defined as the maximum number of children in any vertex. For example, for the tree above the branching coefficient equals $$$2$$$. Your task is to construct a tree with $$$n$$$ vertices such that the sum of the subtree sizes for all vertices equals $$$s$$$, and the branching coefficient is minimum possible."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only input line contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$s$$$ — the number of vertices in the tree and the desired sum of the subtree sizes ($$$2 \\le n \\le 10^5$$$; $$$1 \\le s \\le 10^{10}$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If the required tree does not exist, output «"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"No"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"». Otherwise output «"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"» on the first line, and in the next one output integers $$$p_2$$$, $$$p_3$$$, ..., $$$p_n$$$, where $$$p_i$$$ denotes the parent of vertex $$$i$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3 5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nYes\n1 1 \n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4 42\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nNo\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n6 15\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nYes\n1 2 3 1 5 \n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Below one can find one of the possible solutions for the first sample case. The sum of subtree sizes equals $$$3 + 1 + 1 = 5$$$, and the branching coefficient equals $$$2$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/902ce2fb66aff696e6d4d480375771d203e8b0b89bb6856d5a0920fff8d3efc8.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Below one can find one of the possible solutions for the third sample case. The sum of subtree sizes equals $$$6 + 3 + 2 + 1 + 2 + 1 = 15$$$, and the branching coefficient equals $$$2$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/eff3ee278eb117d93ae68f5a9deb8c25aeba4c43de40adcb0feedb8480477357.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"1098C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1098/problem/C"}